{"cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "claude/rainbow-3d-recovery-m4v347", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"content": "https://atlas.worldlabs.ai/pricing                 404 text/html; charset=utf-8\nhttps://atlas.worldlabs.ai/docs                    308 text/html; charset=utf-8\nhttps://atlas.worldlabs.ai/llms.txt                308 text/html; charset=utf-8\nhttps://api.atlas.worldlabs.ai/openapi.json        401 application/json; charset=utf-8\nhttps://api.atlas.worldlabs.ai/docs                401 application/json; charset=utf-8\n<html><head><meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0; url=https://docs.atlas.worldlabs.ai/llms.txt\" /></head></html>\n# World Labs CLI\n\nUse the World Labs Developer API from a terminal or coding agent with a manually issued API key. The published package has zero npm runtime dependencies; the public SDK is bundled.\n\nWith Node 22 or newer, install the CLI and configure your key:\n\n```sh\nnpm install -g @worldlabsai/cli && worldlabs setup\n```\n\nOn Windows, run these commands in Command Prompt.\n\n`setup` opens the API keys page, prompts you to paste a new key without echoing it, validates it with `assets.list`, and saves it in a plaintext file in your user configuration directory. It can also install the World Labs skills for a coding agent. Use `worldlabs setup --help` for options.\n\n## Onboarding\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[Install CLI] --> B[worldlabs setup]\n    B --> C[Create API key on website]\n    C --> D[Paste key into hidden prompt]\n    D --> E[Validate with assets.list]\n    E --> F[Save credentials file]\n    F --> G[Optionally install the World Labs skills for your coding agent]\n    F --> H[Upload assets and run tasks]\n```\n\nOn the API keys page, choose only the scopes required for your work: task submission, asset upload, operation polling, and asset download. The available choices and descriptions appear in the key creation form. The key belongs to the selected project. Store it as a secret; revoke it from the website if it is exposed or no longer needed.\n\n## Commands\n\n| Command                                                                                     | Purpose                                                                                                 |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `setup [--client <agent>] [--api-key-stdin] [--yes]`                                        | Configure the API key and optionally install the World Labs skills. `--yes` accepts installer prompts.  |\n| `auth login [--no-browser] [--api-key-stdin]`                                               | Open the API keys page, or print its URL for manual opening. `--api-key-stdin` reads a piped key.       |\n| `auth status`                                                                               | Check the key through `assets.list` without printing it. This does not validate every generation scope. |\n| `auth logout`                                                                               | Remove the locally stored key. Revoke the key on the website to invalidate it.                          |\n| `tasks list`                                                                                | List tasks available through the public SDK.                                                            |\n| `tasks run <name> --request file.json [--idempotency-key key] [--wait] [--timeout seconds]` | Submit a task request; optionally wait for its operation.                                               |\n| `assets upload file [--mime type]`                                                          | Upload a local file.                                                                                    |\n| `assets download id --out file`                   