", "type": "boolean"}, "modelParameters": {"$ref": "#/$defs/AtlasChiselModelParameters", "description": "Model-specific parameters for atlasChisel."}, "prompt": {"description": "Text prompt describing the scene.", "minLength": 1, "title": "Prompt", "type": "string"}, "purgeContentOnOperationCompletion": {"anyOf": [{"type": "boolean"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Purge this operation's outputs and the transient uploads it consumed one hour after it finishes. Omitted, the account's setting applies; true raises it for this operation; false is refused when the account already purges. Uploads in the library are never purged by an operation.", "title": "Purgecontentonoperationcompletion"}, "returnDepth": {"default": false, "description": "Return the generated frames as posed RGBD: they are reconstructed together so the depth lands in the request's own camera frame and scale, and every entry in `frames` then carries a `depth` buffer. The targetFrames' own depth is not reconstructed or returned, and context photographs get no depth back. Needs 2 to 256 target frames. Limitation: the depth scale is recovered from the camera centers that joined, so targets that share one center (a pure-rotation rig) and nothing else anchoring them come back with a 0.0 or NaN scale and a success status.", "title": "Returndepth", "type": "boolean"}, "styleReferenceImageAsset": {"anyOf": [{"$ref": "#/$defs/TaskAsset"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Optional style-reference image whose look (medium, palette, lighting) the generated views match; it supplies no camera or geometry, so the prompt and the frames still set the layout."}, "targetFrames": {"description": "The views to generate, in output order, returned in `frames`: one posed frame per view. Each target frame requires a `camera` at 1280x720 with pinhole intrinsics. At most 1440 frames. A frame that carries only its camera generates from the prompt and contextFrames alone. Otherwise each frame carries a depth, an imageAsset (the view's known pixels), or both, and may carry a maskAsset (8-bit grayscale, white where the frame's image and depth are known). For each of `depth`, `imageAsset`, `maskAsset`, and `depth.maskAsset`, include that field on every target frame in the request or omit it from all of them. The model keeps the image where the mask is set and generates the rest, takes frames without masks as fully known, conditions on the depth alone for frames without an image, and for frames without depth keeps the image inside the mask and generates the geometry. A `depth.maskAsset` (8-bit grayscale on the depth grid, white where the depth is known) masks the depth separately from the image. With a depth mask, `maskAsset` marks only the image and requires an `imageAsset`. Both masks read as known above half intensity. Frames carry no depth confidenceAsset.", "items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/AtlasChiselTargetFrameAsset"}, "maxItems": 1440, "minItems": 1, "title": "Targetframes", "type": "array"}, "voxelGridOrientation": {"anyOf": [{"enum": ["world", "gauge"], "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Grid orientation for simplifying depth geometry. 'world' (the default) aligns the grid with the request's world axes so walls aligned with those axes stay flat. 'gauge' aligns the grid with the average camera pose after recentering the scene. Ignored unless voxelSize is set.", "title": "Voxelgridorientation"}, "voxelSize": {"anyOf": [{"minimum": 0, "type": "number"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Side length of the cubes used to simplify depth geometry. Uses normalized scene units, not input distance units: the scene is rescaled so the 90th percentile of inverse depth is approximately 1. The recommended range is 0 to 0.4. Omit or set to 0 to keep the original geometry.", "title": "Voxelsize"}, "webhookUrl": {"anyOf": [{"maxLength": 2048, "type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Where 